                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h3][i]Because, after a tough day, ramming Ork ships while shouting \"Brace for impact!\" is a great way to relieve stress![/i][/h3] \n[hr][/hr]\nhttps://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3812941877 \nUntil recently, I played the tabletop, miniature-based version of this fantastic game; I must admit that switching from turn-based to real-time gameplay was a bit disorienting.\nSetting that aside, I must admit they’ve done an excellent job; they’ve successfully translated all the rules, micromanagement, and features of the \"physical\" game into the PC version.\nThe Imperial Navy campaign is truly epic: you begin as a simple captain—freshly promoted to admiral—with very few ships and limited resources, eventually acquiring larger and more numerous vessels (did someone say battleships?).\nThe plot is particularly engaging, featuring epic and inspiring speeches from your superiors, traitors within your own ranks, and Eldar and Orky pirates raiding your territories.\nAnd let’s not forget your \"dear friends\" from the Chaos faction, who will relentlessly attempt to destroy everything.\nhttps://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3816662663\nCommanding your fleet requires a fair amount of calculated micromanagement, as each ship possesses a wide array of abilities.\nAll ships and their respective crews gain experience and points that can be spent to customize them and enhance their performance.\nYou will decide what to deploy, based on your playstyle or tactics, and according to the points available in the mission briefing.\nThe missions to be carried out are the classic ones from the board game.\nThe Unreal Engine 4 graphics engine will have you drooling as you take in the details of the ships, the battlefield, and—above all—the plasma salvos striking their targets.\nhttps://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3823177815\nIf you loved the \"tabletop\" version of this game and are a fan of RTS games or the Warhammer 40,000 universe—and considering the negligible price of this title—you absolutely shouldn't miss out on it!",
